femto patch for quireink-stardict 0.3.0
Subject: validate definition field framing and encoding

text::decode now returns Result:
- field type bytes must be ASCII letters;
- non-final text fields must be NUL-terminated, a final text field may not
  contain data after its terminator, and binary fields must have a complete
  size prefix and payload (the size addition is checked);
- text fields must be valid UTF-8 (upstream decoded lossily);
- decoded text is capped at 64 KiB;
- fields are processed one at a time instead of being collected first.

Dictionary::lookup propagates the error.

Motivation as for 0002-0004. This is not a complete hostile-input audit.

